\frac{2}{1+Z} = 1 - i \tan x
الطرف الايسر \frac{2}{1+\cos 2x + i \sin 2x}
= \frac{2}{2 \cos^2 x + i(2 \sin x \cdot \cos x)} = \frac{2}{2 \cos x(\cos x + i \sin x)}
= \frac{1}{\cos x(\cos x + i \sin x)} * \frac{\cos x - i \sin x}{\cos x - i \sin x}
= \frac{\cos x - i \sin x}{\cos x(\cos^2 x + \sin^2 x)} = \frac{\cos x - i \sin x}{\cos x(1)}
= \frac{\cos x}{\cos x} - i \frac{\sin x}{\cos x}
= 1 - i \tan x = الطرف الايمن

